    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In a Seattle real estate transaction, an **escrow agent** acts as a neutral third party who holds all funds and documents involving the sale while the deal progresses. This setup ensures that the buyer's loan and earnest money are segregated and protected, preventing the seller from receiving cash before passing title and the buyer from losing money if the deal has contingencies. The money sits with the agent in their own but secure bank account until closing, at which point it is distributed to pay off the buyer's existing loan, pay taxes, and give the net proceeds to the seller.",
