    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok that makes sense. so basically they are just a middleman so no one gets scammed. but is it like... safe? i mean if the agent is just sitting on all that cash, how do i know it's actually being kept secure and not just lost or something? is there any risk with a third party holding everything?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, escrow institutions are highly regulated by state laws and financial oversight to prevent theft or loss, so they are generally considered very secure. Significant funds held by escrow agents are typically collateralized by deposits at high-growth bonds issued by the U.S. Department of the Treasury, which means you have secure government-backed guarantees on your money. Because they operate under strict fiduciary duties, they do not get to decide what to do with the funds without court orders, further minimizing risk for you.",
